WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.950
What replaces the domain join?

2
00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:05.363
Azure Arc gives each
instance an Entra identity.

3
00:00:05.363 --> 00:00:09.662
On SQL Server 2025, that's
the Arc managed identity.

4
00:00:09.662 --> 00:00:14.574
On SQL Server 2022, it's an app
registration with a certificate.

5
00:00:14.574 --> 00:00:18.612
The Azure extension for SQL Server
installs automatically when the

6
00:00:18.612 --> 00:00:22.437
host connects to Arc, and Entra
connections are always encrypted.

7
00:00:22.437 --> 00:00:25.738
The limits matter, and the
old documents missed several.

8
00:00:25.738 --> 00:00:30.826
Failover cluster instances can't use
Entra authentication on any version.

9
00:00:30.826 --> 00:00:35.755
Entra authentication through Arc isn't
available in the US Government Virginia

10
00:00:35.755 --> 00:00:40.170
region, so a GCC tenant uses a commercial
subscription in the same tenant;

11
00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:45.100
the old runbook's Azure Government setup
would never have produced Entra logins.

12
00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:48.363
FIDO2 isn't supported
for SQL Server on Arc.

13
00:00:48.363 --> 00:00:52.218
And granting the instance identity
its Graph permissions needs a

14
00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:56.075
Privileged Role Administrator, so
that step can't sit with the DBAs.

15
00:00:56.075 --> 00:00:59.650
Arc is the program's chosen
path, not the only one:

16
00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:05.425
Microsoft documents a manual setup for
SQL Server 2022 and later on Windows.

17
00:01:05.425 --> 00:01:09.068
Arc wins because it also
carries inventory, policy,

18
00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:12.700
updates and Defender for
the host, which is Book 05.
